 "notes": "José Roberto Arruda (PSD) had his candidacy rejected (TRE-DF, upheld by TSE 5x2 on 2026-09-24); PSD then endorsed Celina Leão. Per spec, governor 1st-round rows use the scenario WITHOUT Arruda; polls that only published an Arruda scenario were skipped for gov_t1: Instituto Opinião 30 Jul-1 Aug (Celina 32.4, Arruda 24.0, Grass 9.8), Datafolha 18-21 Aug (Celina 30, Arruda 28, Grass 11), Quaest 21-24 Aug (Celina 34, Arruda 20, Grass 13), AtlasIntel 27 Aug-1 Sep (Celina 30.7, Grass 29.0, Arruda 14.2), Quaest 4-7 Sep (Celina 35, Arruda 18, Grass 17). Their Celina x Grass runoffs are kept in gov_t2. Instituto Opinião 2t has no BNI published. Celina Leão is PP (Wikipedia still says MDB, outdated). RTBD 'Outros' in gov_t1 is the article's lump for minor candidates. RTBD 2026-09-28 total votes from ncnews.com.br (Gazeta shows only valid votes: Celina 52, Grass 29). Senate: RTBD 2026-09-08 only listed the top five (rest <=2% each), so Ronaldo Fonseca/Outros omitted. Paraná Pesquisas Jul senate uses sum of two votes (and included Rafael Prudente, not running) - excluded. Instituto Veritá poll (PL-commissioned, undated in source, included Izalci) not used. No Jan-Jun 2026 DF polls with the final field were found (en.wikipedia DF pages have no poll tables); coverage is Jul-Sep only; senate is September only.",
